  "FLINK-32613": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-32613",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Disable check for single rowtime attribute for sinks",
    "description": "A common error that users face is the following:\r\n{code}\r\nThe query contains more than one rowtime attribute column [%s] for writing into table '%s'.\r\nPlease select the column that should be used as the event-time timestamp for the \r\ntable sink by casting all other columns to regular TIMESTAMP or TIMESTAMP_LTZ.\r\n{code}\r\n\r\nHowever, not every sink requires the rowtime set on the stream record. For example, the Kafka sink does not use it because it exposes metadata columns. The user can define which column is the rowtime column by projection.\r\n\r\nEither we introduce a config option for disabling this check. Or we come up with an interface that a connector can implement. I would vote for the config option as an easy solution to get rid of this error message.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "3c82386d0e3cc1c61a4e5a8b3161e8af47d700f0",
        "message": "[FLINK-32613] Add ConfigOption for disabling TimestampInserter",
